<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Sallies slips into interim loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Sallies slips into interim loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr loss, (cts)	  3.0 loss     vs    5.0 gain</p>
<p>    Sundry income	    0.21	   vs    0.32</p>
<p>Sundry and rehabilitaion</p>
<p>    expenditure		0.49	   vs    0.55</p>
<p>    Attrib loss		0.28	   vs    0.24</p>
<p>Full name: The South African Land &amp; Exploration Co, owned by Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd (mining producers) .</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had an unfunded obligation evaluated at 17.4 million rand in respect of post-retirement medical aid benefits.</p>
<p>It said this would be initially funded out of the disposal of assets and therefore shareholders should not expect a liquidation dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
